#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm outperforms all classical algorithms for a query problem, but the advantage is quite modest: one query versus two.\n"
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm extends this advantage — and, in fact, it can be used to solve a couple of different query problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"El algoritmo de Deutsch supera a todos los algoritmos clásicos para un problema de consultas, pero la ventaja es bastante modesta: una consulta frente a dos.\n"
"El algoritmo de Deutsch-Jozsa amplía esta ventaja — y, de hecho, puede usarse para resolver un par de problemas de consultas distintos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a quantum circuit description of the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"An additional classical post-processing step, not shown in the figure, may also be required depending on the specific problem being solved.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación se muestra una descripción del algoritmo de Deutsch-Jozsa en forma de circuito cuántico.\n"
"También puede ser necesario un paso adicional de posprocesamiento clásico, no mostrado en la figura, dependiendo del problema específico que se resuelva.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-Jozsa.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Algoritmo de Deutsch-Jozsa](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-"
"quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-Jozsa.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, we haven't actually discussed what problems this algorithm "
"solves; this is done in the two sections that follow.\n"
msgstr ""
"Por supuesto, todavía no hemos explicado qué problemas resuelve este "
"algoritmo; eso se hace en las dos secciones siguientes.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Deutsch-Jozsa problem {#the-deutsch-jozsa-problem}"
msgstr "El problema de Deutsch-Jozsa {#the-deutsch-jozsa-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll begin with the query problem the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm was "
"originally intended to solve, which is known as the *Deutsch-Jozsa "
"problem*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Comenzaremos con el problema de consultas que el algoritmo de Deutsch-Jozsa "
"fue diseñado originalmente para resolver, conocido como el *problema de "
"Deutsch-Jozsa*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The input function for this problem takes the form $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ for an arbitrary positive integer $n.$\n"
"Like Deutsch's problem, the task is to output $0$ if $f$ is constant and $1$ if $f$ is balanced, which again means that the number of input strings on which the function takes the value $0$ is equal to the number of input strings on which the function takes the value $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"La función de entrada para este problema tiene la forma $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ para un entero positivo arbitrario $n.$\n"
"Al igual que en el problema de Deutsch, la tarea consiste en devolver $0$ si $f$ es constante y $1$ si $f$ es balanceada, lo que significa que el número de cadenas de entrada en las que la función toma el valor $0$ es igual al número de cadenas de entrada en las que la función toma el valor $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that, when $n$ is larger than $1,$ there are functions of the form $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ that are neither constant nor balanced.\n"
"For example, the function $f:\\Sigma^2\\rightarrow\\Sigma$ defined as\n"
msgstr ""
"Observa que, cuando $n$ es mayor que $1,$ existen funciones de la forma $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ que no son ni constantes ni balanceadas.\n"
"Por ejemplo, la función $f:\\Sigma^2\\rightarrow\\Sigma$ definida como\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(00) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(01) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(10) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(11) & = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(00) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(01) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(10) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(11) & = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"falls into neither of these two categories.\n"
"For the Deutsch-Jozsa problem, we simply don't worry about functions like this — they're considered to be \"don't care\" inputs.\n"
"That is, for this problem we have a *promise* that $f$ is either constant or balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"no pertenece a ninguna de estas dos categorías.\n"
"Para el problema de Deutsch-Jozsa, simplemente ignoramos funciones como esta — se consideran entradas \"irrelevantes\".\n"
"Es decir, para este problema tenemos la *promesa* de que $f$ es constante o balanceada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Deutsch-Jozsa problem\">\n"
"Input: a function $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Promise: $f$ is either constant or balanced \\\n"
"Output: $0$ if $f$ is constant, $1$ if $f$ is balanced\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Problema de Deutsch-Jozsa\">\n"
"Entrada: una función $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Promesa: $f$ es constante o balanceada \\\n"
"Salida: $0$ si $f$ es constante, $1$ si $f$ es balanceada\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, with its single query, solves this problem in the following sense:\n"
"if every one of the $n$ measurement outcomes is $0,$ then the function $f$ is constant;\n"
"and otherwise, if at least one of the measurement outcomes is $1,$ then the function $f$ is balanced.\n"
"Another way to say this is that the circuit described above is followed by a classical post-processing step in which the OR of the measurement outcomes is computed to produce the output.\n"
msgstr ""
"El algoritmo de Deutsch-Jozsa, con su única consulta, resuelve este problema en el siguiente sentido:\n"
"si todos y cada uno de los $n$ resultados de medición son $0,$ entonces la función $f$ es constante;\n"
"de lo contrario, si al menos uno de los resultados de medición es $1,$ entonces la función $f$ es balanceada.\n"
"Otra forma de expresarlo es que el circuito descrito anteriormente va seguido de un paso de posprocesamiento clásico en el que se calcula el OR de los resultados de medición para producir la salida.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithm analysis {#algorithm-analysis}"
msgstr "Análisis del algoritmo {#algorithm-analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze the performance of the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem, it's helpful to begin by thinking about the action of a single layer of Hadamard gates.\n"
"A Hadamard operation can be expressed as a matrix in the usual way,\n"
msgstr ""
"Para analizar el rendimiento del algoritmo de Deutsch-Jozsa aplicado al problema de Deutsch-Jozsa, conviene comenzar pensando en la acción de una sola capa de puertas Hadamard.\n"
"Una operación Hadamard puede expresarse como una matriz de la manera habitual,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"but we can also express this operation in terms of its action on standard "
"basis states:\n"
msgstr ""
"pero también podemos expresar esta operación en términos de su acción sobre "
"los estados de la base estándar:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"H \\vert 0\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[3mm]\n"
"H \\vert 1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"H \\vert 0\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[3mm]\n"
"H \\vert 1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "These two equations can be combined into a single formula,\n"
msgstr "Estas dos ecuaciones pueden combinarse en una sola fórmula,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H \\vert a \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (-1)^a \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{b\\in\\{0,1\\}} (-1)^{ab} \\vert b\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H \\vert a \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (-1)^a \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{b\\in\\{0,1\\}} (-1)^{ab} \\vert b\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which is true for both choices of $a\\in\\Sigma.$\n"
msgstr "que es válida para ambas opciones de $a\\in\\Sigma.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now suppose that instead of just a single qubit we have $n$ qubits, and a Hadamard operation is performed on each.\n"
"The combined operation on the $n$ qubits is described by the tensor product $H\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes H$ ($n$ times), which we write as $H^{\\otimes n}$ for conciseness and clarity.\n"
"Using the formula from above, followed by expanding and then simplifying, we can express the action of this combined operation on the standard basis states of $n$ qubits like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Supongamos ahora que, en lugar de un solo qubit, tenemos $n$ qubits y se aplica una operación Hadamard a cada uno.\n"
"La operación combinada sobre los $n$ qubits se describe mediante el producto tensorial $H\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes H$ ($n$ veces), que escribimos como $H^{\\otimes n}$ por concisión y claridad.\n"
"Usando la fórmula anterior, y luego expandiendo y simplificando, podemos expresar la acción de esta operación combinada sobre los estados de la base estándar de $n$ qubits de la siguiente manera:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_1 x_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\bigl(H \\vert x_{n-1} \\rangle \\bigr) \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\bigl(H \\vert x_{0} \\rangle \\bigr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{n-1} y_{n-1}} \\vert y_{n-1} \\rangle \\Biggr)\n"
"  \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\n"
"  \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{0}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{0} y_{0}} \\vert y_{0} \\rangle \\Biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"  (-1)^{x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0} \\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_1 x_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\bigl(H \\vert x_{n-1} \\rangle \\bigr) \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\bigl(H \\vert x_{0} \\rangle \\bigr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{n-1} y_{n-1}} \\vert y_{n-1} \\rangle \\Biggr)\n"
"  \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\n"
"  \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{0}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{0} y_{0}} \\vert y_{0} \\rangle \\Biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"  (-1)^{x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0} \\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, by the way, we're writing binary strings of length $n$ as "
"$x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ and $y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0,$ following Qiskit's indexing "
"convention.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nótese que aquí escribimos cadenas binarias de longitud $n$ como "
"$x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ e $y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0,$ siguiendo la convención de "
"indexación de Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This formula provides us with a useful tool for analyzing the quantum circuit above.\n"
"After the first layer of Hadamard gates is performed, the state of the $n+1$ qubits (including the leftmost/bottom qubit, which is treated separately from the rest) is\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta fórmula nos proporciona una herramienta útil para analizar el circuito cuántico anterior.\n"
"Tras aplicar la primera capa de puertas Hadamard, el estado de los $n+1$ qubits (incluido el qubit más a la izquierda/inferior, que se trata de forma independiente del resto) es\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl( H \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\bigl( H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0 \\cdots 0 \\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl( H \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\bigl( H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0 \\cdots 0 \\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "When the $U_f$ operation is performed, this state is transformed into\n"
msgstr "Al aplicar la operación $U_f$, este estado se transforma en\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"through exactly the same phase kick-back phenomenon that we saw in the "
"analysis of Deutsch's algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"exactamente mediante el mismo fenómeno de retroceso de fase que vimos en el "
"análisis del algoritmo de Deutsch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then the second layer of Hadamard gates is performed, which (by the formula "
"above) transforms this state into\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación se aplica la segunda capa de puertas Hadamard, que (según la "
"fórmula anterior) transforma este estado en\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"\\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) + x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0}\n"
"\\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"\\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) + x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0}\n"
"\\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This expression looks somewhat complicated, and not too much can be "
"concluded about the probabilities to obtain different measurement outcomes "
"without knowing more about the function $f.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Esta expresión parece algo complicada, y no se puede concluir mucho sobre "
"las probabilidades de obtener distintos resultados de medición sin conocer "
"más sobre la función $f.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fortunately, all we need to know is the probability that every one of the measurement outcomes is $0$ — because that's the probability that the algorithm determines that $f$ is constant.\n"
"This probability has a simple formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Afortunadamente, lo único que necesitamos saber es la probabilidad de que todos los resultados de medición sean $0$ — porque esa es la probabilidad de que el algoritmo determine que $f$ es constante.\n"
"Esta probabilidad tiene una fórmula sencilla.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl\\vert\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)}\n"
"\\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $f$ is constant}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & \\text{if $f$ is balanced}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl\\vert\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)}\n"
"\\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{si $f$ es constante}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & \\text{si $f$ es balanceada}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In greater detail, if $f$ is constant, then either $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 0$ for every string $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0,$\n"
"in which case the value of the sum is $2^n,$ or $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 1$ for every string $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0,$\n"
"in which case the value of the sum is $-2^n.$\n"
"Dividing by $2^n$ and taking the square of the absolute value yields $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"En detalle, si $f$ es constante, entonces o bien $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 0$ para toda cadena $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0,$\n"
"en cuyo caso el valor de la suma es $2^n,$ o bien $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 1$ para toda cadena $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0,$\n"
"en cuyo caso el valor de la suma es $-2^n.$\n"
"Al dividir por $2^n$ y tomar el cuadrado del valor absoluto obtenemos $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If, on the other hand, $f$ is balanced, then $f$ takes the value $0$ on half"
" of the strings $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ and the value $1$ on the other half, so"
" the $+1$ terms and $-1$ terms in the sum cancel and we're left with the "
"value $0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Si, por otro lado, $f$ es balanceada, entonces $f$ toma el valor $0$ en la "
"mitad de las cadenas $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ y el valor $1$ en la otra mitad, "
"por lo que los términos $+1$ y $-1$ de la suma se cancelan y obtenemos el "
"valor $0.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We conclude that the algorithm operates correctly provided that the promise "
"is fulfilled.\n"
msgstr ""
"Concluimos que el algoritmo opera correctamente siempre que se cumpla la "
"promesa.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical difficulty {#classical-difficulty}"
msgstr "Dificultad clásica {#classical-difficulty}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm works every time, always giving us the correct answer when the promise is met, and requires a single query.\n"
"How does this compare with classical query algorithms for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem?\n"
msgstr ""
"El algoritmo de Deutsch-Jozsa funciona en todo momento, siempre proporciona la respuesta correcta cuando se cumple la promesa y requiere una única consulta.\n"
"¿Cómo se compara esto con los algoritmos de consultas clásicos para el problema de Deutsch-Jozsa?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, any *deterministic* classical algorithm that correctly solves the Deutsch-Jozsa problem must make exponentially many queries:\n"
"$2^{n-1} + 1$ queries are required in the worst case.\n"
"The reasoning is that, if a deterministic algorithm queries $f$ on $2^{n-1}$ or fewer different strings, and obtains the same function value every time, then both answers are still possible.\n"
"The function might be constant, or it might be balanced but through bad luck the queries all happen to return the same function value.\n"
msgstr ""
"En primer lugar, cualquier algoritmo clásico *determinista* que resuelva correctamente el problema de Deutsch-Jozsa debe realizar un número exponencial de consultas:\n"
"se necesitan $2^{n-1} + 1$ consultas en el peor caso.\n"
"El razonamiento es que, si un algoritmo determinista consulta $f$ en $2^{n-1}$ o menos cadenas distintas y obtiene el mismo valor de la función en todas ellas, ambas respuestas siguen siendo posibles.\n"
"La función podría ser constante, o podría ser balanceada pero con mala suerte todas las consultas devuelven el mismo valor de la función.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second possibility might seem unlikely — but for deterministic algorithms there's no randomness or uncertainty, so they will fail systematically on certain functions.\n"
"We therefore have a significant advantage of quantum over classical algorithms in this regard.\n"
msgstr ""
"La segunda posibilidad puede parecer improbable — pero para los algoritmos deterministas no hay aleatoriedad ni incertidumbre, por lo que fallarán sistemáticamente en ciertas funciones.\n"
"Por lo tanto, tenemos una ventaja significativa de los algoritmos cuánticos sobre los clásicos en este sentido.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is a catch, however, which is that *probabilistic* classical algorithms can solve the Deutsch-Jozsa problem with very high probability using just a few queries.\n"
"In particular, if we simply choose a few different strings of length $n$ randomly, and query $f$ on those strings, it's unlikely that we'll get the same function value for all of them when $f$ is balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Existe, sin embargo, una salvedad: los algoritmos clásicos *probabilistas* pueden resolver el problema de Deutsch-Jozsa con alta probabilidad usando solo unas pocas consultas.\n"
"En particular, si simplemente elegimos unas pocas cadenas distintas de longitud $n$ al azar y consultamos $f$ en esas cadenas, es poco probable que obtengamos el mismo valor de la función para todas ellas cuando $f$ es balanceada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be specific, if we choose $k$ input strings $x^1,\\ldots,x^k \\in \\Sigma^n$ uniformly at random, evaluate $f(x^1),\\ldots,f(x^k),$ and answer $0$ if the function values are all the same, and $1$ if not, then we'll always be correct when $f$ is constant, and wrong in the case that $f$ is balanced with probability just $2^{-k + 1}.$\n"
"If we take $k = 11,$ for instance, this algorithm will answer correctly with probability greater than $99.9$%.\n"
msgstr ""
"Más concretamente, si elegimos $k$ cadenas de entrada $x^1,\\ldots,x^k \\in \\Sigma^n$ de manera uniforme aleatoria, evaluamos $f(x^1),\\ldots,f(x^k),$ y respondemos $0$ si todos los valores de la función son iguales y $1$ si no, siempre acertaremos cuando $f$ es constante, y nos equivocaremos en el caso de que $f$ sea balanceada con probabilidad solo $2^{-k + 1}.$\n"
"Si tomamos $k = 11,$ por ejemplo, este algoritmo responderá correctamente con probabilidad superior al $99{,}9$%.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this reason, we do still have a rather modest advantage of quantum over "
"classical algorithms — but it is nevertheless a quantifiable advantage "
"representing an improvement over Deutsch's algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Por esta razón, seguimos teniendo una ventaja más bien modesta de los "
"algoritmos cuánticos sobre los clásicos — pero es, no obstante, una ventaja "
"cuantificable que representa una mejora respecto al algoritmo de Deutsch.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Deutsch-Jozsa with Qiskit {#deutsch-jozsa-with-qiskit}"
msgstr "Deutsch-Jozsa con Qiskit {#deutsch-jozsa-with-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To implement the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm in Qiskit, we'll start by defining a function `dj_query` that generates a quantum circuit implementing a query gate, for a randomly selected function satisfying the promise for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem.\n"
"With a 50% chance, the function is constant, and with 50% change the function is balanced.\n"
"For each of those two possibilities, the function is selected uniformly from the functions of that type.\n"
"The argument is the number of input bits of the function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para implementar el algoritmo de Deutsch-Jozsa en Qiskit, comenzaremos definiendo una función `dj_query` que genera un circuito cuántico que implementa una puerta de consulta, para una función seleccionada aleatoriamente que satisfaga la promesa del problema de Deutsch-Jozsa.\n"
"Con un 50% de probabilidad la función es constante, y con un 50% la función es balanceada.\n"
"Para cada una de estas dos posibilidades, la función se selecciona de manera uniforme entre las funciones de ese tipo.\n"
"El argumento es el número de bits de entrada de la función.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can show the quantum circuit implementation of the query gate using the "
"`draw` method as usual.\n"
msgstr ""
"Podemos visualizar la implementación en circuito cuántico de la puerta de "
"consulta usando el método `draw` como de costumbre.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-"
"algorithm/extracted-outputs/b4a6df3d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Salida de la celda de código "
"anterior](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-"
"algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-"
"outputs/b4a6df3d-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next we define a function that creates the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit, taking a "
"quantum circuit implementation of a query gate as an argument.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación definimos una función que crea el circuito de Deutsch-Jozsa, "
"tomando como argumento un circuito cuántico que implementa una puerta de "
"consulta.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, a function that runs the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit once is defined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Por último, se define una función que ejecuta el circuito de Deutsch-Jozsa "
"una sola vez.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can test our implementation by choosing a function randomly, displaying "
"the quantum circuit implementation of a query gate for this function, and "
"then running the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm on that function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Podemos probar nuestra implementación eligiendo una función aleatoriamente, "
"mostrando la implementación en circuito cuántico de una puerta de consulta "
"para dicha función y ejecutando el algoritmo de Deutsch-Jozsa sobre esa "
