#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The Bernstein-Vazirani problem {#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem}"
msgstr "El problema de Bernstein-Vazirani {#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we'll discuss a problem known as the *Bernstein-Vazirani problem*.\n"
"It's also called the *Fourier sampling problem*, although there are more general formulations of this problem that also go by that name.\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, hablaremos de un problema conocido como el *problema de Bernstein-Vazirani*.\n"
"También se llama *problema de muestreo de Fourier*, aunque existen formulaciones más generales de este problema que también llevan ese nombre.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, let's introduce some notation.\n"
"For any two binary strings $x = x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0$ and $y = y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$ of length $n,$ we define\n"
msgstr ""
"Primero, introduzcamos algo de notación.\n"
"Para cualesquiera dos cadenas binarias $x = x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0$ e $y = y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$ de longitud $n,$ definimos\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y = x_{n-1} y_{n-1} \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus x_0 y_0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y = x_{n-1} y_{n-1} \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus x_0 y_0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll refer to this operation as the *binary dot product*.\n"
"An alternative way to define it is like so.\n"
msgstr ""
"Llamaremos a esta operación el *producto punto binario*.\n"
"Una forma alternativa de definirlo es la siguiente.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is odd}\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"0 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is even}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ es impar}\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"0 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ es par}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that this is a symmetric operation, meaning that the result doesn't change if we swap $x$ and $y,$ so we're free to do that whenever it's convenient.\n"
"Sometimes it's useful to think about the binary dot product $x \\cdot y$ as being the parity of the bits of $x$ in positions where the string $y$ has a $1,$ or equivalently, the parity of the bits of $y$ in positions where the string $x$ has a $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Observa que esta es una operación simétrica, lo que significa que el resultado no cambia si intercambiamos $x$ e $y,$ así que podemos hacerlo cuando nos resulte conveniente.\n"
"A veces es útil pensar en el producto punto binario $x \\cdot y$ como la paridad de los bits de $x$ en las posiciones donde la cadena $y$ tiene un $1,$ o de forma equivalente, la paridad de los bits de $y$ en las posiciones donde la cadena $x$ tiene un $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this notation in hand we can now define the Bernstein-Vazirani "
"problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Con esta notación ya podemos definir el problema de Bernstein-Vazirani.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Bernstein-Vazirani problem\">\n"
"Input: a function $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Promise: there exists a binary string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ for which $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ for all $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Output: the string $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Problema de Bernstein-Vazirani\">\n"
"Entrada: una función $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Promesa: existe una cadena binaria $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ para la que $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ para todo $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Salida: la cadena $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We don't actually need a new quantum algorithm for this problem; the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm solves it.\n"
"In the interest of clarity, let's refer to the quantum circuit from above, which doesn't include the classical post-processing step of computing the OR, as the *Deutsch-Jozsa circuit*.\n"
msgstr ""
"En realidad no necesitamos un nuevo algoritmo cuántico para este problema; el algoritmo de Deutsch-Jozsa lo resuelve.\n"
"Para mayor claridad, llamemos *circuito de Deutsch-Jozsa* al circuito cuántico descrito anteriormente, que no incluye el paso de posprocesamiento clásico de calcular la OR.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithm analysis {#algorithm-analysis-1}"
msgstr "Análisis del algoritmo {#algorithm-analysis-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze how the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit works for a function satisfying the promise for the Bernstein-Vazirani problem, we'll begin with a quick observation.\n"
"Using the binary dot product, we can alternatively describe the action of $n$ Hadamard gates on the standard basis states of $n$ qubits as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para analizar cómo funciona el circuito de Deutsch-Jozsa con una función que satisface la promesa del problema de Bernstein-Vazirani, comenzaremos con una observación rápida.\n"
"Usando el producto punto binario, podemos describir de forma alternativa la acción de $n$ puertas Hadamard sobre los estados de la base estándar de $n$ qubits así:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similar to what we saw when analyzing Deutsch's algorithm, this is because "
"the value $(-1)^k$ for any integer $k$ depends only on whether $k$ is even "
"or odd.\n"
msgstr ""
"De forma similar a lo que vimos al analizar el algoritmo de Deutsch, esto se"
" debe a que el valor $(-1)^k$ para cualquier entero $k$ depende únicamente "
"de si $k$ es par o impar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Turning to the Deutsch–Jozsa circuit, after the first layer of Hadamard "
"gates is performed, the state of the $n+1$ qubits is\n"
msgstr ""
"Volviendo al circuito de Deutsch-Jozsa, después de que se aplica la primera "
"capa de puertas Hadamard, el estado de los $n+1$ qubits es\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The query gate is then performed, which (through the phase kickback "
"phenomenon) transforms the state into\n"
msgstr ""
"A continuación se aplica la puerta de consulta, que (mediante el fenómeno de"
" retroceso de fase) transforma el estado en\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using our formula for the action of a layer of Hadamard gates, we see that "
"the second layer of Hadamard gates then transforms this state into\n"
msgstr ""
"Usando nuestra fórmula para la acción de una capa de puertas Hadamard, vemos"
" que la segunda capa de puertas Hadamard transforma este estado en\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x) + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x) + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we can make some simplifications, in the exponent of $-1$ inside the sum.\n"
"We're promised that $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ for some string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0,$ so we can express the state as\n"
msgstr ""
"Ahora podemos hacer algunas simplificaciones en el exponente de $-1$ dentro de la suma.\n"
"Se nos promete que $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ para alguna cadena $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0,$ por lo que podemos expresar el estado como\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{s\\cdot x + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{s\\cdot x + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $s\\cdot x$ and $x\\cdot y$ are binary values, we can replace the addition with the exclusive-OR — again because the only thing that matters for an integer in the exponent of $-1$ is whether it is even or odd.\n"
"Making use of the symmetry of the binary dot product, we obtain this expression for the state:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dado que $s\\cdot x$ y $x\\cdot y$ son valores binarios, podemos reemplazar la suma por la OR exclusiva — de nuevo porque lo único que importa para un entero en el exponente de $-1$ es si es par o impar.\n"
"Haciendo uso de la simetría del producto punto binario, obtenemos esta expresión para el estado:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(Parentheses have been added for clarity, though they aren't really "
"necessary because it's conventional to treat the binary dot product as "
"having higher precedence than the exclusive-OR.)\n"
msgstr ""
"(Se han añadido paréntesis para mayor claridad, aunque no son estrictamente "
"necesarios porque por convención el producto punto binario tiene mayor "
"precedencia que la OR exclusiva.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "At this point we will make use of the following formula.\n"
msgstr "En este punto haremos uso de la siguiente fórmula.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x) = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x) = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can obtain the formula through a similar formula for bits,\n"
msgstr "Podemos obtener la fórmula a partir de una fórmula análoga para bits,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(a c) \\oplus (b c) = (a \\oplus b) c,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(a c) \\oplus (b c) = (a \\oplus b) c,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"together with an expansion of the binary dot product and bitwise exclusive-"
"OR:\n"
msgstr ""
"junto con una expansión del producto punto binario y la OR exclusiva bit a "
"bit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} x_{n-1}) \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} x_{0}) \\oplus\n"
"(y_{n-1} x_{n-1})  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (y_{0} x_{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} \\oplus y_{n-1}) x_{n-1}  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} \\oplus y_{0}) x_{0} \\\\\n"
"& = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} x_{n-1}) \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} x_{0}) \\oplus\n"
"(y_{n-1} x_{n-1})  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (y_{0} x_{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} \\oplus y_{n-1}) x_{n-1}  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} \\oplus y_{0}) x_{0} \\\\\n"
"& = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This allows us to express the state of the circuit immediately prior to the "
"measurements like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto nos permite expresar el estado del circuito justo antes de las "
"mediciones así:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The final step is to make use of yet another formula, which works for every "
"binary string $z = z_{n-1}\\cdots z_0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"El último paso es hacer uso de otra fórmula más, que es válida para toda "
"cadena binaria $z = z_{n-1}\\cdots z_0.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{z \\cdot x}\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $z = 0^n$}\\\\\n"
"0 & \\text{if $z\\neq 0^n$}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{z \\cdot x}\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{si $z = 0^n$}\\\\\n"
"0 & \\text{si $z\\neq 0^n$}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're using a simple notation for strings that we'll use several more "
"times in the lesson: $0^n$ is the all-zero string of length $n.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Aquí usamos una notación sencilla para cadenas que utilizaremos varias veces"
" más en la lección: $0^n$ es la cadena de todos ceros de longitud $n.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simple way to argue that this formula works is to consider the two cases separately.\n"
"If $z = 0^n,$ then $z\\cdot x = 0$ for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ so the value of each term in the sum is $1,$ and we obtain $1$ by summing and dividing by $2^n.$\n"
"On the other hand, if any one of the bits of $z$ is equal to $1,$ then the binary dot product $z\\cdot x$ is equal to $0$ for exactly half of the possible choices for $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ and $1$ for the other half — because the value of the binary dot product $z\\cdot x$ flips (from $0$ to $1$ or from $1$ to $0$) if we flip any bit of $x$ in a position where $z$ has a $1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Una forma simple de argumentar que esta fórmula es correcta es considerar los dos casos por separado.\n"
"Si $z = 0^n,$ entonces $z\\cdot x = 0$ para toda cadena $x\\in\\Sigma^n,$ por lo que el valor de cada término de la suma es $1,$ y al sumar y dividir entre $2^n$ obtenemos $1.$\n"
"Por otro lado, si alguno de los bits de $z$ es igual a $1,$ entonces el producto punto binario $z\\cdot x$ es igual a $0$ para exactamente la mitad de las posibles elecciones de $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ e igual a $1$ para la otra mitad — porque el valor del producto punto binario $z\\cdot x$ cambia (de $0$ a $1$ o de $1$ a $0$) si invertimos cualquier bit de $x$ en una posición donde $z$ tiene un $1.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we now apply this formula to simplify the state of the circuit prior to "
"the measurements, we obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"Si ahora aplicamos esta fórmula para simplificar el estado del circuito "
"antes de las mediciones, obtenemos\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\vert s \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\vert s \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"owing to the fact that $s\\oplus y = 0^n$ if and only if $y = s.$\n"
"Thus, the measurements reveal precisely the string $s$ we're looking for.\n"
msgstr ""
"dado que $s\\oplus y = 0^n$ si y solo si $y = s.$\n"
"Así, las mediciones revelan exactamente la cadena $s$ que buscamos.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical difficulty {#classical-difficulty-1}"
msgstr "Dificultad clásica {#classical-difficulty-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit solves the Bernstein-Vazirani problem with a"
" single query, any classical query algorithm must make at least $n$ queries "
"to solve this problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mientras que el circuito de Deutsch-Jozsa resuelve el problema de Bernstein-"
"Vazirani con una sola consulta, cualquier algoritmo de consulta clásico debe"
" realizar al menos $n$ consultas para resolver este problema.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be reasoned through a so-called *information theoretic* argument, which is very simple in this case.\n"
"Each classical query reveals a single bit of information about the solution, and there are $n$ bits of information that need to be uncovered — so at least $n$ queries are needed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Esto puede razonarse mediante un argumento denominado *teórico-informacional*, que es muy sencillo en este caso.\n"
"Cada consulta clásica revela un solo bit de información sobre la solución, y hay $n$ bits de información que deben descubrirse — por lo tanto, se necesitan al menos $n$ consultas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is, in fact, possible to solve the Bernstein-Vazirani problem classically by querying the function on each of the $n$ strings having a single $1,$ in each possible position, and $0$ for all other bits, which reveals the bits of $s$ one at a time.\n"
"Therefore, the advantage of quantum over classical algorithms for this problem is $1$ query versus $n$ queries.\n"
msgstr ""
"De hecho, es posible resolver el problema de Bernstein-Vazirani de forma clásica consultando la función en cada una de las $n$ cadenas que tienen un único $1$ en cada posición posible y $0$ en todos los demás bits, lo que revela los bits de $s$ de uno en uno.\n"
"Por lo tanto, la ventaja de los algoritmos cuánticos sobre los clásicos para este problema es de $1$ consulta frente a $n$ consultas.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bernstein-Vazirani with Qiskit {#bernstein-vazirani-with-qiskit}"
msgstr "Bernstein-Vazirani con Qiskit {#bernstein-vazirani-with-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've already implemented the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit above, and here we will make use of it to solve the Bernstein-Vazirani problem.\n"
"First we'll define a function that implements a query gate for the Bernstein-Vazirani problem given any binary string $s.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ya hemos implementado el circuito de Deutsch-Jozsa anteriormente, y aquí lo usaremos para resolver el problema de Bernstein-Vazirani.\n"
"Primero definiremos una función que implementa una puerta de consulta para el problema de Bernstein-Vazirani dada cualquier cadena binaria $s.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-"
"algorithm/extracted-outputs/11861a7e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-"
"of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-"
"algorithm/extracted-outputs/11861a7e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we can create a function that runs the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit on the "
"function, using the `compile_circuit` function that was defined "
